id: pm-vcs-7ydb
title: selfhost.bundle crossed GitHub's 50 MiB per-file warning and grows with every commit toward the 100 MiB per-file limit
description: "On 2026-10-12 a push of the close-out branch warned that selfhost.bundle is 50.53 MB, above the 50 MiB size at which GitHub warns about a single file. The bundle is regenerated for every commit, including tracker-only commits, and grows with history. GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MiB, which would block every PR and release that touches it. Options: an incremental or thin bundle against a recorded base; compressing or pruning objects that self-host verification does not need; moving the full bundle to a release asset and committing only its digest; or Git LFS, which would need evaluating against the self-host contract."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: ci,self-host,size
created_at: "2026-10-12T00:59:40.128Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T01:42:18.043Z"
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "The committed self-host artifact stays well below GitHub's 50 MiB per-file warning as history grows (measured over a projected year of commits), accept:self-host still proves byte-identity of the committed source, and pushes no longer emit the large-file warning."
body: ""
